You really need some form of magic resistance, or you'll likely fall
prey to some horrible instadeath incidence.  Also, given that you have
2 sources of reflection, I'd ditch the shield and start two-weaponing,
preferably with a silver saber in the off-hand if you find one.
Oilskin and and leather gloves are fine, though.  That oilskin cloak
didn't rip in the polytrap, did it?

> I also lost my pet(s), and stepped into a polymorph trap first thing.
> Now I'm a silver dragon. I've heard that I can lay an egg so the baby
> will be my pet. How do I lay an egg though? Any other advice? I'm
> starting to feel too weak to descend further.

You lay eggs with the #sit command, buy only female dragons can lay
eggs, so you might not be able to.  No big deal though, your SDSM will
come back once you polymorph back to human.  Replacing your cloak and
getting MR should be first priority, so a wish for a CoMR would be
good, or you can stick with the oilskin and wish up the Eye of the
Aethiopica, the Platinum Yendorian Express Card or the Eyes of the
Overworld.  Being able to do so depends on what artifacts have been
generated already in your game.

If you can get your hands on a blessed genocide scroll and genocide L
you'd probably be doing yourself a favour, too.  Also, wear a ring of
free action as soon as you find one (paralysis resistance).

Best of luck!
